# Mode Study: A Aeolian (natural minor) (repertoire plan: st-mode-aeolian). An original 16-bar
# melody over a four-bar vamp played four times: Am (x02210) for two bars, then F (133211) and
# G (320003) for one bar each. F, the flat sixth, is the colour of Aeolian: the sad, serious
# sound of natural minor. In the last time round F and G share bar 15, so the tune can come home
# to A in bar 16 (F, G, Am: the classic Aeolian cadence).
# The melody lands on F on a strong beat in bars 3 (beats 1 and 3), 7, 11 and 15, over the F chord.
# Fifth position: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 2 on fret 6 (F on string 2), finger 4 on fret 8.
# The same place on the neck as the Dorian study: only F# becomes F.
title: Mode Study: A Aeolian (natural minor)
